One thing I feel I should note about Nethack's artifacts is, most of
them are taken directly from outside works, often not the kinds of
things that usually get ransacked for the sake of roleplaying games.
For example, Snickersnee comes from The Mikado, a Gilbert and Sullivan
play of all things.

The Magic Mirror of Merlin is another good example.  It comes from The
Faerie Queene, Edmund Spenser's unfinished-yet-still-bloody-huge ode to
Queen Victoria.  It was intended to be a Christian romance (romance in
the older sense), a way of passing moral instruction on to readers
while taking a popular form of the time, that of knightly tales of
adventure.  It is in the Mirror that the soon-to-be warrior maiden
Britomart has her vision of Artigall, the Arthur-figure that she is
fated to marry, and in fact it is with her vision of the man that she
initially falls in love.

Britomart, by the way, is one of the original kick-ass women in English
literature.  Put that magic lance in her arm and she's unstoppable.

